kwalletd6: don't fail networkWallet() when no wallet exists yet

On a fresh profile there are no wallets, so ksecretd answers
ReadAlias("default") with "/" and defaultCollection() reports a failure.
networkWallet() then turns that into a D-Bus error, and that is where
things go wrong for the first app that touches the wallet:

  - qtkeychain probes KWallet by calling networkWallet(). It takes the
    error as "KWallet isn't available" and quietly switches to libsecret,
    which creates a differently named "Default keyring" instead.
  - KWallet::Wallet::NetworkWallet() returns an empty string on the error,
    so libkgapi tries to open a wallet called "" for the Gmail token.

Either way the user never gets the normal "create a new wallet" dialog.
On Termux, where there is no kwallet-pam to create the wallet at login,
KMail is usually that first app, and account setup fails until someone
creates kdewallet by hand in System Settings and logs out and in again.

The old kwalletd simply returned the configured name here, no matter
whether the file existed. Do that again: when there is no default
collection yet, answer with the configured name so the client's open()
call reaches ksecretd and the create dialog shows up as intended.

The error reply was introduced by MR 157 (merged 2026-07-28, in KF 6.31).

--- a/src/runtime/kwalletd/kwalletd.cpp
+++ b/src/runtime/kwalletd/kwalletd.cpp
@@ -1013,8 +1013,14 @@
     const QString defaultWallet = m_backend->defaultCollection(&ok);
 
     if (!ok) {
-        sendErrorReply(QDBusError::Failed, QStringLiteral("Failed to query default collection"));
-        return {};
+        // Nothing to look up yet: on a brand new profile ksecretd has no
+        // collections at all, so the "default" alias doesn't resolve. That is
+        // not an error from the caller's point of view, it just means the wallet
+        // hasn't been created. Hand back the configured name (kdewallet unless
+        // the user changed it) like the old kwalletd did, otherwise qtkeychain
+        // decides KWallet is unusable and libkgapi ends up trying to open a
+        // wallet with an empty name, and the first wallet never gets created.
+        return KWallet::Backend::networkWallet();
     }
     return defaultWallet;
 }
@@ -1030,8 +1036,9 @@
         const QString defaultWallet = m_backend->defaultCollection(&ok);
 
         if (!ok) {
-            sendErrorReply(QDBusError::Failed, QStringLiteral("Failed to query default collection"));
-            return {};
+            // Same story as in networkWallet() above: no wallet exists yet,
+            // so fall back to the configured name instead of failing.
+            return KWallet::Backend::localWallet();
         }
         return defaultWallet;
     }
